7","[[24,16],[1,0],[19,8],[3,18],[26,23],[25,4],[9,5],[25,26],[9,10],[25,24],[12,4],[6,9],[26,24],[6,14],[0,11],[11,17],[1,18],[22,20],[7,10],[15,18],[5,8],[22,25],[20,14],[22,13],[16,23],[10,2],[10,11],[14,17],[24,7],[22,18],[4,1],[25,5],[23,11],[13,21],[15,1],[13,15],[23,21],[7,9],[3,8]]"],"out":"[[8,19],[4,12],[10,2]]","g":1},{"in":["27","[[17,8],[18,21],[18,2],[9,8],[26,3],[11,15],[9,11],[4,2],[8,0],[5,0],[9,12],[4,1],[17,20],[4,6],[4,5],[12,13],[9,7],[22,25],[24,23],[1,19],[10,20],[6,1],[16,18],[13,6],[11,14],[0,1],[10,13],[20,16],[25,7],[2,5],[18,1],[9,21],[22,7],[3,25],[14,23],[21,23],[4,25],[16,24],[20,21]]"],"out":"[[11,15],[1,19],[3,26],[25,3]]","g":1},{"in":["3","[[1,0],[2,1],[0,2]]"],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["13","[[10,7],[4,2],[5,6],[7,6],[8,12],[0,11],[7,5],[8,2],[5,2],[11,10],[3,9],[4,0],[1,7],[3,10],[7,12],[12,4],[10,1],[8,0]]"],"out":"[[3,9],[10,3]]","g":1},{"in":["4","[[0,1],[0,3],[3,2],[1,3],[1,2]]"],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["35","[[4,25],[32,28],[4,10],[22,11],[12,32],[18,9],[7,31],[7,0],[2,21],[20,8],[18,34],[28,14],[13,0],[14,8],[14,27],[22,16],[26,4],[1,8],[3,2],[18,0],[7,16],[33,14],[7,14],[27,30],[30,19],[5,26],[25,14],[21,15],[17,31],[24,7],[20,29],[20,2],[10,23],[6,8]]"],"out":"[[31,17],[7,31],[22,11],[16,22],[7,16],[32,12],[28,32],[14,28],[20,29],[21,15],[2,21],[2,3],[20,2],[8,20],[8,1],[8,6],[14,8],[30,19],[27,30],[14,27],[14,33],[10,23],[4,10],[26,5],[4,26],[25,4],[14,25],[7,14],[7,24],[0,7],[0,13],[18,9],[18,34],[0,18]]","g":1},{"in":["4","[[2,1],[1,3],[2,0],[1,0]]"],"out":"[[1,3]]","g":1},{"in":["5","[[1,4],[0,1],[1,3],[2,1]]"],"out":"[[1,4],[1,3],[1,2],[0,1]]","g":1},{"in":["3","[[1,0],[2,0],[1,2]]"],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#542656:1c7373fac8ddc5e8\"","perf":{"label":"n = 80,000, 96,000 links","gen":"int a0 = 80000; List<List<Integer>> a1 = new ArrayList<>(); for (int i = 0; i + 1 < a0; i++) a1.add(Arrays.asList(i, i + 1)); for (int i = 0; i + 2 < a0; i += 5) a1.add(Arrays.asList(i, i + 2)); Collections.shuffle(a1, new Random(7));","call":"List<List<Integer>> got = s.criticalConnections(a0, a1); List<Long> k = new ArrayList<>(); for (List<Integer> e : got) k.add((long) Math.min(e.get(0), e.get(1)) * 200000 + Math.max(e.get(0), e.get(1))); Collections.sort(k); Object r = k;"},"refMs":54}],"lesson":"advanced-graphs","statement":"There are `n` servers numbered `0` to `n − 1`, joined by undirected `connections`, where `connections[i] = [a, b]` links servers `a` and `b`. Every server can reach every other server, directly or through others.\n\nA **critical connection** is one whose removal would leave some server unable to reach some other server.\n\nReturn all critical connections, in any order. Each connection may be written as `[a, b]` or `[b, a]`.","constraints":["2 <= n <= 1e5","n − 1 <= connections.length <= 1e5","0 <= a, b <= n − 1","a != b","There are no repeated connections","The network is connected"],"hints":["Removing each edge and checking connectivity with BFS works, but that is O(E · (V + E)), far too slow for 10⁵ edges. You need to find all such edges in one traversal.","An edge is critical exactly when it is not on any cycle. During a DFS, give each node a discovery time. Track low[u]: the earliest discovery time reachable from u's subtree using at most one back edge.","For a tree edge u → v, if low[v] > disc[u], nothing under v can reach u or above without that edge, so it is a bridge. Skip the edge back to the parent when updating low."],"explain":"Servers 0, 1 and 2 form a triangle, so removing any one of those three links still leaves the others connected. Server 3 hangs off server 1 by a single link, so removing [1,3] cuts it off. The only critical connection is `[[1,3]]`."},
