"out":"[[1,11],[11,1]]","g":1},{"in":["[[262888554,582400865]]"],"out":"[[262888554,582400865]]","g":1},{"in":["[[660652272,328712092],[192147502,660652272],[660652272,838573294],[509874171,192147502],[333326580,660652272],[333326580,509874171],[328712092,84442611],[328712092,333326580],[838573294,660652272],[660652272,333326580]]"],"out":"[[328712092,333326580],[333326580,509874171],[509874171,192147502],[192147502,660652272],[660652272,333326580],[333326580,660652272],[660652272,838573294],[838573294,660652272],[660652272,328712092],[328712092,84442611]]","g":1},{"in":["[[16,24]]"],"out":"[[16,24]]","g":1},{"in":["[[19,7],[9,23],[7,9],[23,7],[7,19],[19,9],[9,7],[7,23],[23,19]]"],"out":"[[19,9],[9,7],[7,23],[23,19],[19,7],[7,9],[9,23],[23,7],[7,19]]","g":1},{"in":["[[18,8],[8,15],[10,18],[18,10],[15,10],[10,8]]"],"out":"[[18,10],[10,8],[8,15],[15,10],[10,18],[18,8]]","g":1},{"in":["[[8,14],[14,8]]"],"out":"[[8,14],[14,8]]","g":1},{"in":["[[10,27],[13,10],[1,2],[2,8],[2,20],[10,13],[20,2],[27,1],[8,13],[13,18]]"],"out":"[[10,13],[13,10],[10,27],[27,1],[1,2],[2,20],[20,2],[2,8],[8,13],[13,18]]","g":1},{"in":["[[14,24],[7,11],[12,18],[7,18],[12,7],[30,18],[24,11],[7,12],[18,4],[7,9],[11,30],[18,14],[11,12],[18,7],[4,7],[11,18],[18,11]]"],"out":"[[7,12],[12,7],[7,18],[18,11],[11,18],[18,7],[7,11],[11,12],[12,18],[18,14],[14,24],[24,11],[11,30],[30,18],[18,4],[4,7],[7,9]]","g":1},{"in":["[[4,12]]"],"out":"[[4,12]]","g":1},{"in":["[[11,19],[13,23],[23,19],[23,13],[5,13],[5,23],[13,5],[11,23],[23,11],[19,23],[19,5],[23,5],[5,19],[11,13],[19,11],[13,11]]"],"out":"[[11,13],[13,11],[11,23],[23,5],[5,19],[19,11],[11,19],[19,5],[5,23],[23,13],[13,5],[5,13],[13,23],[23,19],[19,23],[23,11]]","g":1},{"in":["[[2,21],[1,20],[21,16],[19,2],[13,19],[20,1],[1,22],[22,13],[13,20],[16,13],[19,16],[1,19],[16,1]]"],"out":"[[1,19],[19,16],[16,1],[1,22],[22,13],[13,19],[19,2],[2,21],[21,16],[16,13],[13,20],[20,1],[1,20]]","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#4:5b5c98ef514dbfa5\"","perf":{"label":"100,000 pairs","gen":"int N = 50000; int[] lab = BCB.perm(N, 0); int[] ord = BCB.perm(2 * N, 0); int[][] a0 = new int[2 * N][]; for (int k = 0; k < 2 * N; k++) { int i = ord[k] % N, step = ord[k] < N ? 1 : 7; a0[k] = new int[] { lab[i] * 20000, lab[(i + step) % N] * 20000 }; }","call":"long[] want = new long[a0.length]; for (int i = 0; i < a0.length; i++) want[i] = (long) a0[i][0] * 1000000001L + a0[i][1]; Arrays.sort(want); int[][] got = s.validArrangement(a0); boolean ok = got.length == want.length; for (int i = 0; ok && i + 1 < got.length; i++) ok = got[i][1] == got[i + 1][0]; if (ok) { long[] have = new long[got.length]; for (int i = 0; i < got.length; i++) have[i] = (long) got[i][0] * 1000000001L + got[i][1]; Arrays.sort(have); ok = Arrays.equals(want, have); } Object r = ok;"},"refMs":125}],"lesson":"advanced-graphs","statement":"You are given a 2D array `pairs` where `pairs[i] = [start, end]`. An arrangement of the pairs is **valid** if, for every index `i` from `1` to `pairs.length − 1`, the end of the previous pair equals the start of the current one: `arrangement[i − 1][1] == arrangement[i][0]`.\n\nReturn any valid arrangement that uses every pair exactly once. The input is guaranteed to have one.","constraints":["1 <= pairs.length <= 1e5","pairs[i].length == 2","0 <= start, end <= 1e9","start != end","No two pairs are the same","A valid arrangement exists"],"hints":["Treat each number as a node and each pair as a directed edge from start to end. A valid arrangement is a path that uses every edge exactly once: an Euler path.","An Euler path starts at the node whose out-degree is one more than its in-degree, if such a node exists; otherwise the path is a cycle and can start anywhere with an outgoing edge.","Hierholzer's algorithm: from the start, keep following unused edges; when a node has none left, add it to the answer and back up. The nodes come out in reverse order. Use an explicit stack, since the path can be 10⁵ edges long."],"explain":"[11,9] ends at 9, [9,4] starts at 9 and ends at 4, [4,5] starts at 4 and ends at 5, and [5,1] starts at 5. Each end matches the next start, so `[[11,9],[9,4],[4,5],[5,1]]` is valid."}
]
